WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Why is the slope of x squared always 2x?

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:08.430
Take a point, and another a tiny step h further on.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.770
The rise is 2xh plus h squared. Divide by the run, h.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.950
That leaves just 2x plus h.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:19.630
Now let h shrink towards nothing.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:23.550
What is left is the slope, everywhere: 2x.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.010
Check at x equals 2: the tangent slope is 4.
